Arrived around 5 PM, first meal of the trip.

After being seated, the waiter provided a menu and pen/paper.

Each dish was numbered, and some dishes had pictures for reference.

Overall, the meal was quite good, except the dining area was not air-conditioned.

There was a slight breeze that day, but it didn't affect the dining experience.

@Cold Corn Salad: Not bad~ Slightly spicy, refreshing.

@Grilled Pork Neck: Highly recommended 👍 Charcoal grilled aroma~ Properly prepared, no porky smell. A perfect match with sticky rice (long wait time).

@Stir-fried Water Spinach: Good wok hei (wok aroma), crisp enough.

@Seafood Fried Rice: I thought it was okay, the cucumber on the side was juicy and refreshing.

@Sour Sausage: Delicious~ Unlike roadside vendors, not too sour, eaten with ginger and lettuce~ Special.

The menu also has Northeastern-style earthenware pot; I'll try that next time.

This bar is conveniently located right next to the BTS Skytrain 💛
Plus, they have DJs/live music (depending on the day) 🎧🎼 It's perfect for chatting, enjoying drinks, and having a great time. You can easily walk across from The Mall afterwards – super convenient! (But if you're planning to come on a weekend, I recommend calling to reserve a table beforehand~)

//Whispering: The cocktails they make are all delicious! I love them and want to go back to try more! 🪄🍸

I'd been wondering about it for a while, but it was terrible ^^;
First of all, the draft beer was awful. I'm sure they didn't clean it properly.
Also, we arrived after 8pm on the day, and there was almost nothing to order 💧 No chicken or beef, and the oden we ordered surprisingly had no daikon radish. The other dishes were also 70% of the size we'd expected... None of us were able to finish our meal, so we went to Seiryu Ramen on the way home. It was delicious.

The menu is so extensive that it can be confusing for foreigners, but you can enjoy delicious, freshly fried potatoes! 

I wish the menu was simpler^^;

There are about three tables next to it, so I recommend eating freshly cooked food there!
